## 6. Grid specification

- Column system: 12-col logical grid inside the framed content column, no gutters between bordered cells (cells touch; borders are the gutters).
- Feature grid: 2 cols (6+6). Ownership: 3 cols (4+4+4). Pricing: 4 cols (3+3+3+3). Highlights: 3 cols x 2 rows. Platform downloads: 3 cols. Tutorials and community: 3 cols. App family: 3 cols x 2 rows.
- Heading blocks sit in the left 8 columns (max-width ~820px); paragraph max-width 480-560px.
- Hero text is centered; section headers are left-aligned (home hero, app hero, CTAs are the centered exceptions).
- Breakpoints: >=1280 full layout; 1024-1279 hide section index, keep ruler; 768-1023 grids drop to 2 cols (pricing 2x2, family 2x3); <768 single column, nav collapses to logo + hamburger + LAUNCH APP button.

---

## 7. Behavior

- Marquee: CSS translateX loop, duplicated content, pauses on hover.
- Scroll-spy rail: IntersectionObserver on each [data-section]; sets active label and ruler number.
- Ruler: tick labels move with scroll; value = Math.round(scrollY / pageHeight * 50).
- Sticky nav: position fixed, always visible; dropdown opens on hover/click.
- Feature video cells: autoplay muted loop playsinline; lazy-load below the fold.
- Pricing toggle: JS swaps data-monthly / data-yearly attributes.
- Library filter: buttons set data-filter; cards toggle hidden by data-category; count label updates.
- OS detection: navigator.userAgent picks the primary download button and tags that column "YOUR SYSTEM".
- Copy buttons: navigator.clipboard.writeText, label briefly changes to "COPIED".
- Theme toggle: toggles [data-theme] on <html>, stored in localStorage.
- Hover micro-interactions: border color --line -> --line-strong, button fill transitions 150ms; no scale or bounce animations.
- Section entrance: optional 12px fade-up on scroll, 300ms.

